Pin torch to a CPU-only build to avoid pulling in CUDA deps
Pin torch to a CPU-only build to avoid pulling in CUDA deps

torch is a transitive dependency of sentence-transformers. PyPI's
default Linux wheel bundles the full CUDA/cuDNN/cuBLAS/triton
toolchain, which is dead weight on a GPU-less host like Render's free
tier — it just makes the build much slower and larger for no benefit,
since sentence-transformers here only ever runs on CPU.

Adds --extra-index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu (which
supplements PyPI rather than replacing it, so every other dependency
still resolves normally) and pins torch==2.3.1+cpu specifically. A
bare version pin isn't enough — PyPI's CUDA-bundled wheel shares the
same version number, and pip doesn't reliably prefer one index over
another for identical versions, so only the exact "+cpu" build
forces the CPU-only wheel.

