Prepare backend for Render deployment

- CORS: allow_origins now always includes localhost (dev) plus any
  origins listed in the new ALLOWED_ORIGINS env var (comma-separated),
  so a deployed frontend URL (e.g. Vercel) never needs to be
  hardcoded — it's just set once known.
- Drop the unused httpx dependency from requirements.txt (never
  imported anywhere; was added speculatively for a "future use" that
  never happened).
- Add backend/.python-version (3.11.9) so Render's Python-native
  runtime matches what this app was built and tested against.
- Add backend/scripts/prefetch_model.py: downloads the
  sentence-transformers model during the build step instead of lazily
  on the first indexing request. On ephemeral-disk hosts this avoids
  a live ~90MB Hugging Face download stacking on top of normal
  cold-start latency for whoever's first request lands after a
  deploy.
- Documented ALLOWED_ORIGINS in .env.example.

GROQ_API_KEY and all other config were already environment-variable
only (via pydantic-settings), with .env correctly gitignored and
never committed — confirmed, no code change needed there.

